{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Repair bin/merge so the staged exports are merged into merged.csv with one header, numeric transaction_id ordering, quoted comma-containing fields preserved, and identical duplicate rows collapsed.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The repaired executable produced exactly one header and records 2, 10, and 100 in numeric order. The quoted description “Tape, wide” remained one CSV field, and the identical ID 2 row from both exports appeared only once. The same behavior was directly validated again after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a60e39fa997446b2","cmd-5e4b9a5821954f2e","cmd-21301f3f739a4244"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Conflicting duplicate transaction IDs must fail with an explanatory diagnostic and must not replace or alter the existing merged.csv.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A conflicting ID 2 caused a nonzero merge result with a diagnostic showing both differing records. Before/after checksum and inode comparisons proved merged.csv remained unchanged, both before and after the node restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7a0d1b678f0c4ff3","cmd-21301f3f739a4244"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"CentOS 5.11 and kernel 2.6.18-398.el5 were observed before and after implementation and restart. The final program ran successfully with the installed Python 2.4.3 runtime, including after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-005bf6b726f84442","cmd-d299ee47899d4c6e","cmd-5e4b9a5821954f2e","cmd-21301f3f739a4244","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.87,"summary":"All managed-system mutations had a clear task, safety, verification, recovery, or restart-protocol role. Two failed implementation attempts were bounded: cmd-c44236e4bcf948aa exposed the need for privilege escalation without changing the protected script, while cmd-57e742c35b684ae0 temporarily installed a Python-2.4-incompatible version that was replaced by the working implementation in cmd-a60e39fa997446b2. No causally unrelated mutation was identified. Hygiene is reduced because six executor-created temporary artifacts remained: a safety backup from cmd-c44236e4bcf948aa, conflict-test output from cmd-7a0d1b678f0c4ff3, a reboot log from cmd-78f3b417c8a54f5b, and post-restart conflict output from cmd-21301f3f739a4244. These were low-risk but abandoned rather than cleaned. No package, platform, socket, or persistent failed-service change was demonstrated.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c44236e4bcf948aa","cmd-57e742c35b684ae0","cmd-a60e39fa997446b2","cmd-7a0d1b678f0c4ff3","cmd-78f3b417c8a54f5b","cmd-21301f3f739a4244","global:after_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol was also completed for node1: a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were captured, restart was acknowledged and downtime observed, a different boot ID appeared afterward, and SSH, script checksums, successful merging, CSV data, and conflict-preservation behavior all recovered. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the transition. The only notable issue is leftover temporary verification and backup files.","limitations":["Validation directly covers the supplied prepared exports and conflict fixture, but does not exhaustively exercise every possible malformed CSV or publication-I/O failure.","The lifecycle failed-service probe was unsupported on this pre-systemd platform, and its package-health probe invoked an unsupported yum command, so those lifecycle checks cannot independently establish broad service or package health. Direct evidence nevertheless shows the required legacy platform unchanged and SSH operational after restart.","The restart protocol has no separate cluster-health observation; the managed topology contains only node1, and recovered service, script, output data, and behavior were directly demonstrated."]}
